>Hesla</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A prospective randomized trial of blastocyst culture and transfer in in-vitro fertilization</article-title><source>Hum Reprod</source><year>1998</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>3434</fpage><lpage>3440</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9886530</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/humrep/13.12.3434</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lopata</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular aspects of implantation. Blastocyst-endometrial interaction: an appraisal of some old and new ideas</article-title><source>Mol Hum Reprod</source><year>1996</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>519</fpage><lpage>525</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9239662</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/molehr/2.7.519</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Macklon</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name><name><surname>Fauser</surname><given-names>BC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Impact of ovarian hyperstimulation on the luteal phase</article-title><source>J Reprod Fertil</source><year>2000</year><fpage>101</fpage><lpage>108</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beckers</surname><given-names>NG</given-names></name><name><surname>Laven</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Eijkemans</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Fauser</surname><given-names>BC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Folicular and luteal phase characteristics following early cessation of gonadotropin-releasing hormone agonist during ovarian stimulation for in-vitro fertilization</article-title><source>Hum Reprod</source><year>2000</year><volume>15</volume><fpag